  <script>
/* =========================================================================
   COURSE_DATA
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   This is the ONLY file you should need to edit to add or update content.
   Readings and videos live directly in this file / this folder — nothing
   is embedded from other websites.

   Structure:
   COURSE_DATA.timeline = [                  <- ONE master timeline shared
     { id: "t1", date: "1865", title: "...",     by every lesson in the
       details: "...", category: "..." },        whole course, in order.
     ...                                          "category" is optional.
   ]

   COURSE_DATA.inquiries = [                 <- big, recurring questions for
     { id: "inq1", question: "..." },            the WHOLE YEAR — several
     ...                                          lessons across different
                                                   units point at the same
                                                   one via inquiryFocus below.
   ]

   COURSE_DATA.units = [
     {
       id:     "unit1"            <- unique, no spaces, used in URLs
       number: 1                  <- for display ("Unit 1")
       title:  "Unit title"
       era:    "1865-1877"        <- short date range shown on the tab
       lessons: [
         {
           id:    "1-1"                    <- unique across the whole site
           number:"1.1"                    <- for display
           title: "Lesson title"
           inquiryFocus: [ "inq1", "inq3" ]   <- ids from COURSE_DATA.inquiries
                                                  that this lesson speaks to.
                                                  Shown near the top of the
                                                  lesson. Leave the array
                                                  empty if none apply yet.
           objectives: [                       <- learning objectives, shown
             { id: "1-1-o1", text: "..." },        as a bulleted list near
             ...                                    the top of the lesson.
           ]                                       Give each one a unique id
                                                     (scoped to this lesson is
                                                     fine, e.g. "1-1-o1") so
                                                     questions can tag it.
           needToKnow field no longer exists — see keyTerms below.
           mentions: [ "e5", "e6", "e1" ]   <- ids from COURSE_DATA.entities:
                                                EVERY person/topic/event/term
                                                this lesson touches on. Shown
                                                as tappable chips under
                                                "People, Topics & Events";
                                                tapping one lists every OTHER
                                                lesson that also mentions it.
           keyTerms: [ "e5", "e6" ]         <- subset of the ids above that
                                                matter enough to also feature
                                                under "What You Need to Know"
                                                for THIS lesson specifically.
                                                Same entities, same data —
                                                keyTerms just controls which
                                                ones get the extra emphasis
                                                here.

           readings: [
             {
               title: "...",
               source: "...",
               note: "...",
               text: "Full reading text goes right here as a plain string.
                       Separate paragraphs with a blank line (two newlines)
                       and it will be split into <p> tags automatically.
                       Start a paragraph with '# ' for a Heading 1, '## '
                       for a Heading 2, or '> ' for a block quote — anything
                       else is a normal paragraph.",
               questions: [
                 {
                   afterParagraph: 0,             <- 0 = right after the 1st
                                                      paragraph, 1 = after the
                                                      2nd, etc.
                   type: "multiple_choice",       <- or "short_answer"
                   objectiveIds: [ "1-1-o1" ],    <- optional: ids from this
                                                      lesson's objectives list,
                                                      shown as tags on the card
                   image: "images/chart.jpg",     <- optional: a photo, map, or
                                                      chart shown under the prompt
                   prompt: "...",
                   choices: [ "...", "...", "..." ],
                   correctIndex: 1,               <- 0-based index into choices
                   explanation: "..."             <- shown after answering, optional
                 },
                 ...
               ]
             },
             ...
           ]

           assessment: [                    <- standalone questions for the
             {                                 whole lesson, shown at the end
               type: "multiple_choice",         under "Check Your Understanding"
               objectiveIds: [ "1-1-o1" ],       (same shape as reading questions,
               image: "images/chart.jpg",        including optional objectiveIds
               prompt: "...",                    and image)
               choices: [ "...", "...", "..." ],
               correctIndex: 0,
               explanation: "..."
             },
             {
               type: "short_answer",
               objectiveIds: [ "1-1-o3" ],
               prompt: "...",
               sampleAnswer: "..."           <- revealed on tap, not graded
             },
             ...
           ]

           videos: [
             {
               title: "...",
               length: "12:04",
               note: "...",
               src: "videos/your-file.mp4"   <- path to a video file placed
                                                  in the videos/ folder next
                                                  to this site. Nothing is
                                                  pulled from YouTube/Vimeo/etc.
             },
             ...
           ]

           images: [
             {
               title: "...",
               note: "...",
               files: [ "images/photo.jpg" ]           <- one file = single image
             },
             {
               title: "...",
               note: "...",
               files: [ "images/a.jpg", "images/b.jpg", "images/c.jpg" ]
                                                          <- 2+ files = gallery,
                                                             shown with Prev/Next
                                                             in the popup
             },
             ...
           ]

           timelineFocus: [ "t2", "t3" ]   <- ids from COURSE_DATA.timeline
                                               that this lesson's events
                                               belong to.
         },
         ...
       ]
     },
     ...
   ]

   To add a lesson: copy an existing lesson block, give it a new unique id,
   fill in the fields, save. It will automatically appear as a step in the
   Previous/Next flow and be reachable at lesson.html?id=YOUR-ID

   To add a historical event: add it to COURSE_DATA.timeline (give it a new
   unique id, keep the list in chronological order), then reference that id
   in whichever lesson(s) it belongs to via timelineFocus.

   To add a person/topic/event/term: add it to COURSE_DATA.entities (give it
   a new unique id, a category of "person", "topic", or "event", and
   a "definition"). Optionally add "image": "images/yourfile.jpg" — shown
   when someone taps through for details. Then list that id under
   "mentions" on whichever lesson(s) touch on it, and ALSO under "keyTerms"
   if it's important enough to feature under "What You Need to Know" for
   that particular lesson. The same entity can be reused across as many
   lessons as apply — that's what lets you look up every lesson a person,
   topic, or term appears in.

   To add a course inquiry: add it to COURSE_DATA.inquiries (give it a new
   unique id), then reference that id from inquiryFocus on whichever
   lesson(s) it applies to — the same inquiry can (and should) be reused
   across multiple lessons and units over the course of the year.

   To add a video: drop the video file (.mp4 works everywhere) into the
   videos/ folder next to index.html, then point "src" at it, e.g.
   src: "videos/reconstruction-overview.mp4"

   To add images: drop the file(s) into the images/ folder next to
   index.html, then list them under "files". One file makes it a single
   image; two or more makes it a gallery with Prev/Next in the popup.

   Leave an array empty ( needToKnow: [] ) if a lesson has nothing for that
   section yet — the site will just skip that section.
   ========================================================================= */

const COURSE_DATA = {
  courseTitle: "US History II",
  courseSubtitle: "Reconstruction to the Present",

  // ---- People, topics, events & terms mentioned across the course --------
  // Defined once here; each lesson lists which ids it mentions (see
