// ==========================================================================
// SITE THEMES
// A theme is a set of colors (and, optionally, fonts) the whole site is
// drawn with. Each UNIT can have its own look:
//   - In the sheet: add a "Theme" column to your Units tab and type a
//     theme's id (e.g. navy) or its name (e.g. Navy & Brass).
//   - On the site: Teacher View -> Themes tab has a dropdown per unit. What
//     you pick there overrides the sheet and is saved for everyone.
//   - Leave both blank and the unit uses DEFAULT_THEME_ID.
//
// To add your own theme, copy one block below, give it a new id, a label,
// and change the colors. What each color is used for:
//   --stamp           the header bar and main accent (buttons, labels, card shadows)
//                     — the biggest splash of color, so choose it first
//   --parchment       page background        --parchment-dim  darker page tint
//   --card            cards and popups       --ink            main text, borders
//   --ink-soft        secondary text
//   --brass           highlights, numbers    --brass-light    lighter highlight
//   --forest          second accent (green)  --focus          links and focus rings
//   --rule            thin divider lines     --shadow         drop shadows
//   Texture (optional, all subtle): --page-pattern is a faint tile over the page,
//   --header-pattern a texture on the header bar, --title-pattern the same on
//   section tabs, --edge-pattern a decorative strip hanging under the header
//   (--edge-height is its height). Each takes a CSS url("data:image/svg+xml,...").
//   Leave them out and a theme stays flat color, as before.
//   Loading icon (optional): --loading-glyph is a Font Awesome icon's code (as "\\f6e2")
//   and --loading-anim one of loading-bob / bounce / pulse / swing / spin / spin-slow /
//   wobble / fly / orbit / blink / pageflip, shown on the "Loading lesson" screen.
//   Header animation (optional): banner: "snow" | "leaves" | "bats" | "lights" | "bunting"
//   plays a gentle animated scene in the header, only while the page is scrolled to the very top.
//   bannerImage: "https://.../anything.gif" shows your own GIF/image there as well.
// Fonts (optional): --font-display is the big uppercase headings,
// --font-heading the small caps labels and buttons, --font-body the reading
// text. If a theme uses a Google Font the site doesn't already load, put the
// part after "css2?" of its Google Fonts link in googleFonts.
// Keep --ink dark against --parchment and --card, and --stamp dark enough
// for light text on the header bar, so everything stays readable. Make each
// theme's --stamp a clearly different color so units look distinct.
// ==========================================================================
// ==========================================================================
// THEME SETTINGS (the "Themes" tab)
// Add a tab called Themes, then add a row to the Sheet Index tab: Name = Themes,
// GID = that tab's gid. One row per theme, columns (header names not case sensitive):
//   Name    the theme's name or id, e.g. Halloween or halloween (either works)
//   Type    Student / Unit / Seasonal — groups the picker ("Everyday", "Eras & units", "Seasonal").
//           A theme with Units is only offered in those units; one with Months is only
//           offered in those months; Seasonal themes are never offered in a Sensitive Lesson.
//   Hidden  check it to take the theme out of the students' picker (any theme). A hidden
//           theme still works if you set it as a lesson/unit default.
//   Units   (optional) unit numbers or ids this theme belongs to, e.g. 3 or 3, 4. It is that
//           unit's default look and only students in those units can pick it.
//   Months  (optional) when the theme is available: Oct, Oct-Nov, Dec-Jan, or 10, 11 ...
//           Seasonal themes are never the default — only a choice in the picker.
// NOTHING IS LOCKED: students can always switch to any visible theme (a button at the
// bottom right). What a student sees by default, in order: their own pick -> Teacher View's
// pick for the unit -> the Theme set on the
// lesson/unit (or a Themes-tab Units match) -> the site default.
// Mark a lesson (or unit) as a Sensitive Lesson on the Lessons/Units tab to switch seasonal
// themes off for it. Test a month by adding ?themeMonth=10 to the page address.
// Themes missing from the tab use the built-in Type below (first six = Student, five seasonal).
// ==========================================================================
// Used until (or unless) the Themes tab loads; the tab replaces this completely.
const DEFAULT_THEME_SETTINGS = {
