  <script>
/* =========================================================================
   RESPONSES_CONFIG
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Where student answers get sent. Leave submitUrl blank and answer
   logging is silently disabled — students can still answer questions
   normally, nothing just gets recorded anywhere.

   Reading from a spreadsheet (Units, Entities, your lesson tabs, etc.) is
   simple — Google publishes a sheet as a plain CSV link you can fetch.
   WRITING back to a spreadsheet from a static site needs something extra,
   since there's no server here to do that safely. The standard way to
   do it without setting up your own backend is a small script attached
   directly to your spreadsheet — Google Apps Script — that receives
   requests and appends rows for you.

   SETUP (one-time):
     1. Open the spreadsheet you want responses saved into.
     2. Extensions → Apps Script.
     3. Delete whatever starter code is there, and paste in the script
        from the "Apps Script for logging answers" section of this
        project (ask Claude for it again if you don't have it handy).
     4. Deploy → New deployment.
     5. Click the gear icon next to "Select type" → Web app.
     6. Description: anything, e.g. "Student Answers Logger".
     7. Execute as: Me.
     8. Who has access: Anyone.
     9. Click Deploy, then authorize the permissions it asks for.
     10. Copy the "Web app URL" it gives you — paste it below.

   That URL is NOT a link to open in a browser — it's an endpoint the
   site sends data to quietly in the background. A "Responses" tab will
   appear in your spreadsheet automatically the first time a student
   answers something.
   ========================================================================= */

const RESPONSES_CONFIG = {
  submitUrl: "https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfycbwVvgQ_TOvNcS14ft6wikEWiHfncMn7UiECs7j_jgqh0waLvwDiZdvRrXNK_JZ1tDiXRQ/exec"
};

